'''Big Brother 25''' is the 25th season of the broadcasted edition of ''[[Big Brother U.S. (franchise)|Big Brother (U.S.)]]'' and the 29th season overall.
==Background==
[[File:BB25 Key Art Logo.jpg|thumb|200px|Promotional Logo]]
As with the past few seasons, this season was first announced by the show itself ahead of an official renewal announcement from CBS, with a casting call being aired during the Final Three recap episode of ''[[Big Brother 24 (US)]]'', the penultimate episode of the season. The same casting call was later tweeted out that night<ref>https://twitter.com/CBSBigBrother/status/1573476301456822272</ref> with the "#BB25" hashtag and a link to the CBS casting webpage,<ref>https://www.bigbrothercasting.tv/home</ref> which was also updated to say that applications for season 25 are open. The official renewal announcement was made on finale night of BB24.<ref>https://twitter.com/JCMoonves/status/1574218978502873088</ref>
===Development===
Due to the [[wikipedia:2023 Writers Guild of America strike|2023 Writers Guild of America strike]] impacting their fall schedule, CBS announced on May 22nd, 2023 that ''Big Brother 25'' and [[w:c:thechallenge:The Challenge: USA 2|''The Challenge: USA 2'']] would be getting delayed debuts in August instead of July as they did the year prior. BB25 specifically was set to air on Wednesday, August 2nd with a special 90-minute live premiere at 8 PM EST, continuing with its usual Wednesday-Thursday-Sunday schedule. However, airing on Wednesdays in the fall would clash with the already announced [[w:c:survivor:Survivor 45|''Survivor 45'']] and [[w:c:amazingrace:The Amazing Race 35|''The Amazing Race 35'']], which were confirmed to be getting 90-minute episodes for their entire seasons just weeks ahead of the BB25 announcement.<ref>https://ew.com/tv/big-brother-delayed-start-summer-2023-all-new-cast/</ref> When CBS officially announced their fall schedule on July 17, 2023, it was revealed that the schedule clashing would be resolved by moving the second half of BB25 from Wednesdays to Tuesdays, but remaining in its 8 PM EST timeslot. In addition, the Thursday episodes would be pushed up from 9 PM EST to 8 PM EST, while the Sunday episodes would be pushed back from 8 PM EST to 10 PM EST.<ref>https://twitter.com/CBS/status/1681018180687515648</ref>

The last time a writers strike impacted CBS scheduling was in [[wikipedia:2007–08 Writers Guild of America strike|2007-2008]], which led to ''[[Big Brother 9 (US)]]'' airing that winter, with ''[[Big Brother 10 (US)]]'' taking the usual summer slot in its place. Instead of adding a second main season for the year or going for a fourth ''Celebrity Big Brother'' season, CBS repeated the approach they took the last time ''Big Brother'' had to be delayed to an August premiere, which was with ''[[Big Brother 22 (US)]]'' running from August to late October due to the [[The Impact of COVID-19 on Big Brother|COVID-19 pandemic]].

The promotional material for this season started being released as early as May 2023, and highlighted the series as a whole instead of just the last few seasons, honing in on the anniversary aspect of 25 seasons.<ref>https://twitter.com/JoshTalksBB/status/1658993314132119552</ref><ref>https://twitter.com/CBSBigBrother/status/1660692900496437250</ref>

The season was reported to be lasting into November, which would mark the return to 90+ day seasons since ''[[Big Brother 21 (US)]]'' clocked in 99 days, before the shift down to 85 days the following season.<ref>https://www.yahoo.com/entertainment/cbs-eyes-reality-paramount-originals-012220011.html</ref><ref>https://twitter.com/rbbq/status/1672316916592181248</ref> It was later confirmed that the season would last for 100 days for the first time ever, with finale night set to be on Thursday, November 9, 2023.<ref>https://twitter.com/sharontharp/status/1684610424505761805</ref>

After it was announced that ''[[Big Brother Canada 11]]'' would be doing away with their Live Feeds, a statement was immediately released, informing the American audience that the Live Feeds would remain intact for BB25.<ref>https://ew.com/tv/big-brother-live-feeds-season-25/</ref> On August 1, 2023, it was announced that the Live Feeds would be aired for free on their own channels within Pluto TV, with limited ad breaks shown throughout. The Live Feeds would continue to air on Paramount+ with a subscription and no ads.<ref>https://deadline.com/2023/08/big-brother-season-25-live-feeds-pluto-tv-paramount-plus-1235452160/</ref>
===Casting===
This season saw a return to in-person casting calls following their [[The Impact of COVID-19 on Big Brother|hiatus during the pandemic]].<ref>https://bigbrothernetwork.com/big-brother-25-casting-open-call-auditions/</ref>
===The House===
The house photos were unveiled ahead of the August 2, 2023, premiere, showcasing a unique "Big Brother Multiverse" theme inspired by a universe of twists and alternate realities. The house was divided into zones with names like Scary-Verse, Comic-Verse, Scramble-Verse, and Humili-Verse, each influencing the design of various rooms.<ref>https://bigbrothernetwork.com/big-brother-25-house-tour-video-photo-gallery/</ref><ref>https://www.paramountpressexpress.com/cbs-entertainment/shows/big-brother/</ref><ref>https://www.etonline.com/big-brother-season-25-twist-revealed-see-what-familiar-faces-are-returning-to-shake-up-the-house</ref>
